PRACTICAL 1: SIMPLE ASP.NET CORE WEB APPLICATION

Step 1. Open Visual Studio 2019 and choose Create a new project.
Step 2. Search for ASP.NET Core Web App, select it, and click Next.
Step 3. Set the project name to HelloWebApp, choose a folder, and click Create.
Step 4. Choose .NET Core and select Web Application (Model-View-Controller) or Empty. Create the project.
Step 5. Open Controllers/HomeController.cs. Use the first code below to display Hello World.
Step 6. Save and press F5 (or IIS Express) to run the application.
Step 7. For the form example, replace the controller with the form controller code and put the view code in Views/Home/Index.cshtml.
Step 8. Run again, enter a name, and click Submit. Check that the welcome message appears.

HomeController.cs - Hello World

using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
namespace HelloWebApp.Controllers
{
    public class HomeController : Controller
    {
        public IActionResult Index()
        {
            return Content("Hello World from ASP.NET Core!");
        }
    }
}

HomeController.cs - Simple Form

using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
namespace HelloWebApp.Controllers
{
    public class HomeController : Controller
    {
        public IActionResult Index()
        {
            return View();
        }

        [HttpPost]
        public IActionResult Index(string name)
        {
            ViewBag.Message = "Welcome " + name;
            return View();
        }
    }
}

Views/Home/Index.cshtml

<form method="post">
    <label>Name:</label>
    <input type="text" name="name" />
    <button type="submit">Submit</button>
</form>

@if(ViewBag.Message != null)
{
    <h2>@ViewBag.Message</h2>
}

Expected result: The app starts, the Home page loads, the form accepts input, and a message such as 'Welcome John' is displayed.


